# Reach the local stack from another device (README "Access from another
# device", TODO.md D19/D20). This is a LAYER on top of .env, not a full env
# file:
#
#   docker compose --env-file .env --env-file .env.remote up -d -V
#
# `scripts/remote-up.sh lan|ngrok` writes .env.remote from this file; by hand,
# copy it to .env.remote (git-ignored) and edit the one line below.
#
# WEB = the public URL that reaches port 3000. The browser talks to the API
# through that same origin (/backend/*, D20), so nothing else is needed.
# LAN example:   WEB=http://192.168.1.42:3000
# ngrok example: WEB=https://<your-domain>.ngrok-free.dev
WEB=http://192.168.1.42:3000

# Both derive from the line above (Compose expands ${WEB} inside this file).
# The session cookie is bound to NEXTAUTH_URL, so the host must ALSO open the
# stack at ${WEB}, not at localhost. FRONTEND_URL drives every browser-facing
# URL the API builds (email links, photos, the stub Checkout page).
NEXTAUTH_URL=${WEB}
FRONTEND_URL=${WEB}
